    <!-- 1. TARGET WORKFLOW -->
    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="workflow" class="doc-h2">1. The target workflow (matches the talk)</h2>
            <ol class="doc-body">
                <li><strong>AI works in a worktree.</strong> Agent (in-app AI, Hermes, or browser AI editor) edits files
                    in the worktree checkout and commits there. The repo-level
                    <code>.git/hooks/pre-commit</code> (perl -c + gitleaks) gates every commit — same rule for all AIs.</li>
                <li><strong>Testing happens in the worktree.</strong> The branch's own instance runs on its port;
                    <code>script/test_gate.sh</code> runs there and must be green before merge.</li>
                <li><strong>Human reviews on main (3001).</strong> The main instance dashboard lists worktree branches,
                    shows a per-file diff <em>with context</em> through the shared diff view, lets the admin
                    view/edit/stage changes, then <strong>Merge to main</strong>.</li>
                <li><strong>Human approval is mandatory before AI code enters main.</strong> Any commit containing
                    AI-generated or mixed-provenance code must carry an explicit human audit approval
                    (<a href="/todo/details?record_id=1993" class="doc-link">todo #1993</a>) before it can be merged
                    into or pushed to <code>main</code>. The AI may commit <em>only</em> inside the worktree; entry
                    into <code>main</code> is gated on the human view &rarr; edit &rarr; approve flow
                    (<a href="/todo/details?record_id=1991" class="doc-link">todo #1991</a>).</li>
                <li><strong>Human pushes to GitHub.</strong> After merge, main pushes <code>origin/main</code>.</li>
            </ol>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc" class="doc-link">↑ Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- 2. CURRENT STATE -->
    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="current" class="doc-h2">2. Current state (what exists, what's missing)</h2>
            <table class="doc-table">
                <tr class="doc-tr-alt">
                    <th class="doc-th">Capability</th>
                    <th class="doc-th">Today</th>
                    <th class="doc-th">Gap</th>
                </tr>
                <tr><td class="doc-td">AI commit in worktree (gated)</td><td class="doc-td">✅ pre-commit hook covers it</td><td class="doc-td">—</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="doc-td">Test in worktree</td><td class="doc-td">✅ test_gate.sh + per-branch port</td><td class="doc-td">not yet a required pre-merge step</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="doc-td">Main sees worktree branch</td><td class="doc-td">✅ shared .git — branch IS visible</td><td class="doc-td">no UI to pick/inspect it</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="doc-td">Contextual diff review</td><td class="doc-td">partial (suggest_message reads diff)</td><td class="doc-td">no shared per-file view/edit/stage UI (see &sect;3.5)</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="doc-td">Merge worktree &rarr; main</td><td class="doc-td">❌ not in app</td><td class="doc-td"><code>merge</code> not in Util::Git whitelist</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="doc-td">Push main &rarr; GitHub</td><td class="doc-td">✅ push exists (deploy.sh pushes currently disabled)</td><td class="doc-td">wire as explicit human action</td></tr>
            </table>
