    <!-- 3. CHANGES REQUIRED -->
    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="changes" class="doc-h2">3. Changes required</h2>

            <h3 id="c31" class="doc-h3">3.1 Util::Git — add merge + worktree to the whitelist</h3>
            <p class="doc-body">Add <code>merge</code> to <code>%ALLOWED_SUBCMD</code> with a tight flag allow-list
            (<code>--no-ff</code>, <code>--no-commit</code>, <code>--abort</code>, <code>--squash</code>). Add
            <code>worktree</code> (subcommands <code>list</code>, <code>prune</code> only — never <code>add</code> from the
            app). Keep the no-shell / no-chdir / whitelist enforcement already in place.</p>

            <h3 id="c32" class="doc-h3">3.2 Admin::Git — worktree branch list + diff review endpoints</h3>
            <ul class="doc-body">
                <li><code>/admin/git/worktrees</code> (GET): list branches that have a worktree dir, with ahead/behind vs main and last commit.</li>
                <li><code>/admin/git/review/&lt;branch&gt;</code> (GET): for the chosen worktree branch, return a
                    structured per-file diff (<code>git diff main...&lt;branch&gt;</code>) with N lines of context,
                    file mode, and the worktree path. The shared diff-view widget renders it (see &sect;3.5).</li>
                <li><code>/admin/git/review/edit</code> (POST, admin-only): accept a corrected file body for a single
                    changed file (admin edits before merge); writes it into the worktree checkout and stages it there,
                    so the human's edits are part of the merged result. (Guard: only within the worktree dir;
                    path validated against the diff file list — no free-form paths.)</li>
            </ul>

            <h3 id="c33" class="doc-h3">3.3 Admin::Git — the merge + push action (human-gated)</h3>
            <ul class="doc-body">
                <li><code>/admin/git/merge_to_main</code> (POST, admin-only):
                    <ol>
                        <li>Switch main repo to <code>main</code> (already have switch).</li>
                        <li>Run <code>script/test_gate.sh</code> against the worktree path; if not green, refuse merge
                            with the failing output.</li>
                        <li>Require a covering human audit approval (<a href="/todo/details?record_id=1993" class="doc-link">#1993</a>)
                            before merging; refuse if missing/stale/doesn't cover the current diff.</li>
                        <li><code>git merge --no-ff &lt;branch&gt;</code> (via the new whitelist entry).</li>
                        <li>On conflict, abort and report; human resolves in worktree then retries.</li>
                    </ol>
                </li>
                <li><code>/admin/git/push_main</code> (POST, admin-only): <code>git push origin main</code> from the main
                    repo — the explicit "push to GitHub" the human performs.</li>
            </ul>

            <h3 id="c34" class="doc-h3">3.4 Same rules for Hermes / browser AI editor</h3>
            <p class="doc-body">The rule "AI commits only in the worktree, never to main" is enforced by two things that already cover
            any AI: (a) the pre-commit hook is repo-level and shared by the worktree; (b) the app provides
            <strong>no merge/push path for non-admins</strong> — <code>merge_to_main</code> and <code>push_main</code>
            are admin-only. For Hermes/browser editors, the constraint is operational: they must be told to edit only
            inside the worktree checkout path, exactly like the in-app AI. Add a one-line note to the AI dev-security
            sub-project (ai_dev_security_quality_plan.tt) stating any AI — in-app, Hermes, or browser — commits solely
            in the worktree and is merged only via the human merge action.</p>

            <h3 id="c35" class="doc-h3">3.5 Single shared diff-view component (one page to maintain) — DECIDED</h3>
            <p class="doc-body">There is exactly <strong>one</strong> diff <em>renderer</em>; every surface embeds it and only adds its
            own buttons around it. We do <strong>not</strong> build a separate diff viewer per page, and we do
            <strong>not</strong> designate the AI2 editor's chat-coupled file as the "canonical" copy for others to
            import — that would drag editor-only state (Ace instance, chat suggestion, auto-refresh poll) into pages
            that have none of it. Instead the renderer itself is extracted to a neutral, surface-agnostic widget.</p>

            <p class="doc-body"><strong>Canonical widget:</strong> <code>root/static/js/git-diff-viewer.js</code> with a clean API,
            e.g. <code>renderDiff(targetEl, diffText, { scope, editable, onApprove, onReject })</code>. It owns only the
            diff rendering: unified or side-by-side layout, syntax highlighting, line numbers, and the payload shape.
            It is fed by the <strong>single existing</strong> backend endpoint
            <code>GET /admin/git/review/&lt;branch&gt;</code> (already returns the diff) — the same endpoint is reused
            for a single file (parameterised by path) and for a whole branch. No surface re-implements rendering.</p>

            <p class="doc-body"><strong>Surfaces are consumers of the widget, and legitimately differ ONLY at the affordance layer
            (the buttons / shell around the diff), never at the renderer:</strong></p>
            <ul class="doc-body">
                <li><strong>Git Dashboard (<code>/admin/git</code>)</strong> Working Tree rows: each created/modified
                    file gets a <em>View diff</em> link that opens the shared widget for that one file, read-only, with
                    just a close button. The dashboard reuses <code>git-diff-viewer.js</code> (loaded via
                    <code>js_load.tt</code>); no inline <code>&lt;script&gt;</code>.</li>
                <li><strong>Merge review (<code>/admin/git/review/&lt;branch&gt;</code>)</strong>: embeds the same widget
                    and layers the edit + record-approval controls (<a href="/todo/details?record_id=1993"
                    class="doc-link">todo #1993</a>) around it.</li>
                <li><strong>AI2 editor review pane</strong> (<code>root/ai2/editor/editing_widget_popup.tt</code>):
                    embeds the same widget and layers its editor-specific controls — Approve/Reject applies a chat
                    suggestion into the Ace instance, plus the file auto-refresh poll. This is the <em>only</em> surface
                    that needs those controls; they live in the editor's own module, not in the shared widget.</li>
                <li><strong>Commit-message preview / <code>suggest_message</code></strong>: reuses the same diff payload
                    shape so there is a single diff source of truth in <code>Comserv::Util::Git</code>.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="doc-body"><strong>The only legitimate reasons surfaces differ:</strong> (1) different interaction model — glance vs
            edit+approve vs apply-to-Ace; (2) different embedding shell — editor popup vs admin page; (3) different data
            scope — single file vs whole branch vs staged vs working-tree, expressed as a parameter, not a new component.
            None of these justify a second diff renderer. This is the resolution of the former open question — see &sect;6.</p>

            <h3 id="c36" class="doc-h3">3.6 Mandatory human view &rarr; edit &rarr; approve before AI code enters main — DECIDED</h3>
            <p class="doc-body">The former open question (view-only vs edit-before-merge) is <strong>resolved</strong>: the human flow
            is <strong>view, edit, and approve</strong> before the AI's code may be merged to <code>main</code>:
            the admin opens the shared diff view for a worktree branch, may edit individual files (writes into the
            worktree checkout, staged there), and must record an explicit audit approval
            (<a href="/todo/details?record_id=1993" class="doc-link">todo #1993</a>) before merge/push. This is owned by
            <a href="/todo/details?record_id=1991" class="doc-link">todo #1991</a> (the diff review + edit surface).</p>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc" class="doc-link">↑ Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- 4. SAFETY -->
    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="safety" class="doc-h2">4. Safety / guardrails</h2>
            <ul class="doc-body">
                <li><code>main</code> and <code>master</code> are protected: the app refuses to delete/force-push them
                    (already in <code>get_branch_details</code>).</li>
                <li>Merge is admin-only, requires a green test gate AND a covering human audit approval; the app never auto-merges.</li>
                <li>All git ops stay no-shell, no-chdir, whitelisted (existing Util::Git contract).</li>
                <li>Worktree edits are path-confined to the diff's file list — no arbitrary file writes.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc" class="doc-link">↑ Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- 5. SEQUENCING -->
    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="sequencing" class="doc-h2">5. Sequencing (proposed)</h2>
            <ol class="doc-body">
                <li><strong>Step 1:</strong> Util::Git whitelist: add <code>merge</code> + <code>worktree</code> (low risk).</li>
                <li><strong>Step 2:</strong> Admin::Git endpoints: worktrees list + review diff (read-only, safe).</li>
                <li><strong>Step 3:</strong> Build the shared <code>git-diff-viewer.js</code> widget (&sect;3.5) and wire it into the
                    Git Dashboard working-tree rows (<a href="/todo/details?record_id=1991" class="doc-link">#1991</a>).</li>
                <li><strong>Step 4:</strong> Admin::Git: review/edit (admin edits a file) + merge_to_main gated on test_gate AND approval
                    (<a href="/todo/details?record_id=1993" class="doc-link">#1993</a>).</li>
                <li><strong>Step 5:</strong> Admin::Git: push_main (explicit human push to GitHub).</li>
                <li><strong>Step 6:</strong> Document the all-AI rule in ai_dev_security_quality_plan.tt.</li>
            </ol>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc" class="doc-link">↑ Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- 6. DECISIONS -->
    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-100">
            <h2 id="decisions" class="doc-h2">6. Decision log (open questions resolved)</h2>
            <p class="doc-body"><strong>Q (v0.1):</strong> should the worktree diff review UI let the admin <em>edit</em> individual files
            before merge, or only <em>view + stage/unstage</em>? — <strong>ANSWER (v0.2/v0.3): view, edit, and approve.</strong>
            The human may edit files in the worktree checkout before merge (&sect;3.6), but merge/push into <code>main</code>
            is blocked until an explicit human audit approval exists and covers the current diff
            (<a href="/todo/details?record_id=1993" class="doc-link">todo #1993</a>). Separately, the diff UI is a
            <strong>single shared component</strong> (&sect;3.5), not one per surface.</p>
            <p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#toc" class="doc-link">↑ Back to Top</a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

